<title>BELGIUM: ASTURIENNE SAYS CHAIRMAN DIED TUESDAY.</title>
<headline>ASTURIENNE SAYS CHAIRMAN DIED TUESDAY.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-06-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Belgian non-ferrous metals and minerals group Cie Royale Asturienne des Mines said on Wednesday chairman Jacques van der Schueren died on Tuesday, aged 75.</p>
<p>As well as serving as Asturienne's chairman, van der Schueren was a board member of Asturienne's Swiss parent company Harwanne , an honary deputy governor of Societe Generale de Belgique and honary president of Tractebel and its gas distribution arm Distrigas .</p>
<p>Van der Schueren was also a former Belgian economics minister and member of parliament.</p>
<p>-- Nick Antonovics, Brussels Newsroom +32 2 287 6817, Fax +32 2 230 7710</p>
